KG42.register("rules-f0be793021f65b790fb12b89",{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R010","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The LEM includes electricity and hydrogen as traded energy products. Scope: The proposed local energy market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"The proposed local energy market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E17"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The LEM includes electricity and hydrogen as traded energy products. Scope: The proposed local energy market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E17"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract / Nomenclature","anchor_text":"in which electricity and hydrogen are traded. Players in the LEM Pconsist of renewable distributed g","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Abstract—The proliferation of distributed energy resources entails efficient market mechanisms in distribution-level networks. This paper establishes a local energy market (LEM) framework, in which electricity and hydrogen are traded. Players in the LEM consist of renewable distributed generators (DGs), loads, hydrogen vehicles, and a hydrogen storage system (HSS) operated by an HSS agent. An iterative LEM clearing method is proposed based on the merit order principle. Players submit offers/bids with consideration of their own preferences and profiles according to the utility functions. The decentralized LEM clearing process not only avoids complex calculation induced by the centralized decision process, but also preserves players’ privacy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"electricity by hydrogen. Hydrogen can be purchased from a hy drogen station (HS) and sold to hydroge","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The contributions of this work include the following. First, a LEM framework is established, in which both electricity and hydrogen are traded. Players of the LEM include renewable DGs, flexible and non-flexible loads, electric vehicles (EVs), HVs and an HSS. Since the LEM is organized at distribution level, players can choose to participate in the LEM or trade with DisCo/HS."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The source-backed rule is a categorical product-scope declaration. The supplied passages identify traded energy carriers but define no decision variable or operational decision whose optimization role can be represented as x. The only frozen node is product.local_energy, a categorical market-product node rather than a variable.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed coefficient, constant, price, capacity, unit conversion, or other parameter is defined in the supporting passages for this product-scope rule. The graph also contains no parameter node for this rule, so no theta can be added without inventing unsupported mathematics."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","quote":"This paper establishes a local energy market (LEM) framework, in which electricity and hydrogen are traded."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E17","quote":"First, a LEM framework is established, in which both electricity and hydrogen are traded."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"52c4382a84183a5429d4f5df35649b55c9add0f5984e9d316379827e691b05ea","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule represents a qualitative market-product scope: the proposed LEM includes electricity and hydrogen as traded energy products. The supporting passages state this product composition explicitly, but they contain no equation, optimization variable, parameter, inequality, objective, or algebraic condition to formalize. The graph has only the categorical node product.local_energy with no edges, so the rule is treated as a non-mathematical product-definition rule rather than as an unsupported mathematical relation. The B evidence remains unreviewed; this assessment relies only on the supplied quotations and does not claim independent source review.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
